      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T20:54:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Write \"sector size\" or \"crypto sector size\", instead of \"block size\".\n\nAlso, have you considered using a sector size of 4096 bytes instead of the default of 512 bytes?  4096-byte sectors are much more efficient, especially with HCTR2 which has more per-message overhead than XTS.\n\nFYI, selecting 4096-byte sectors requires that `sector_size\u003d4096` and `iv_large_sectors` be appended to the dm-crypt target parameters; see the dm-crypt documentation.  And regardless of this, the device-mapper API still requires that sizes be given in multiples of 512 bytes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "752dd637fdad296d4bedf90313d63b5a310ce1c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
